<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- July 11-13.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- July 11-13.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the July 11-13 U.S. box office, according to data issued Monday by Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		     Three-day gross   Cumulative Gross </p>
<p>1.Men in Black		 $30,062,317	 $139,584,970</p>
<p>2.Contact			$20,584,908	 $  ---- </p>
<p>3.Face/Off		     $12,332,309	 $ 71,772,555 </p>
<p>4. Hercules		    $ 8,339,217	 $ 66,492,048 </p>
<p>5. My Best Friend's </p>
<p>			 Wedding $ 8,321,580	 $ 83,502,316 </p>
<p>6. Out to Sea		  $ 4,155,935	 $ 14,680,413 </p>
<p>7. Batman &amp; Robin	    $ 4,085,749	 $ 98,795,842 </p>
<p>8. Con Air		     $ 2,891,449	 $ 89,903,753 </p>
<p>9. A Simple Wish	     $ 2,731,880	 $  ---- </p>
<p>10 The Lost World	    $ 1,350,900	$ 221,055,524</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Men in Black&quot; is released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. Sony's TriStar studio released &quot;My Best Friend's Wedding.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Contact&quot; and &quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Face/Off&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Hercules&quot; and &quot;Con Air&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;A Simple Wish&quot; and &quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; are released by Universal Studios, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Out to Sea&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
